Author: ember arlynx <cmrx64@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Oct 27 01:26:58 2026 -0400

    sandbox: a confined child confines itself — Landlock, seccomp and a connector replace bwrap (CLIENT-48)
    
    On Linux, sandbox::command now returns the program itself with a pre-exec step. The launcher
    builds a Landlock ruleset whose rules hold O_PATH descriptors of the policy's paths, two seccomp
    programs, and (for a policy with connect entries) a seqpacket connector. Between fork and exec
    the child applies them to itself: setsid, a SIGKILL parent-death signal, no_new_privs,
    landlock_restrict_self, seccomp. No helper binary, no user namespace, no mount, no openat2, so it
    composes with systemd's own hardening: RestrictNamespaces=yes, ProtectKernelTunables=yes,
    ProcSubset=pid, RestrictSUIDSGID=yes and MemoryDenyWriteExecute=yes all stay on, and a unit
    filter of @system-service only needs @sandbox added (measured on hbox with the new
    deploy/live/confined-unit.sh: host serve and a member's follower ran as transient system units
    with the demo box's full drop-ins, and the member created, wrote and read back).
    
    What a confined child can no longer do: open anything outside its grants (EACCES), exec anything
    but its program, its exec entries and their interpreters, execute a file it wrote, make a socket,
    fork, signal another process, or connect to a socket its policy does not name. Connect goes
    through the connector, which dials only the policy's entries and hands the socket over
    SCM_RIGHTS; nd, the probe and the Lean resident's sock.c use it. A runnable file inside a hidden
    tree is granted as that one inode, so a Host under /home runs with /home hidden (TESTGROUND-4).
    
    Breaking, and what re-emits: EXEC_FILTERED and CONNECT_FILTERED are gone (both platforms filter
    both). ConnectOverlap, SocketInGrant and GrantUnlisted are gone from the sandbox and from
    Hosting.LaunchFailure (codes 14-16; launcher/src/generated.rs re-emitted). killed_by_signal is
    the signal alone (no 128+N). sandbox/apparmor/nd-bwrap is deleted and nothing is installed for
    confinement. Instead a kernel without Landlock ABI 3, or a unit filter without @sandbox, now
    refuses every launch as MechanismMissing("landlock"). The units drop AF_NETLINK (deploy/units
    re-emitted). Tests that asserted bwrap's mount scaffolding (ENOENT for hidden names, listable
    socket directories) now assert EACCES and "not listed". Test stubs that forked now fork nothing.
    The demo box tarball must be rebuilt at this commit.
    
