The main finding is a gap in write confinement: the child can change permissions and timestamps on reachable files owned by its UID outside the write grant, unless the outer systemd mount policy blocks it. The connector also re-resolves socket paths on every request without repeating the launch-time ownership checks. That provides authority over a socket name, not a pinned server identity.

